# Mutation cases for "a completion or a failure that names where it came from needs no
# script engine when no `<finalize>` is waiting for it" under the Kotlin runtime
# (SCE Accepted Subset §2.15; docs/adr/0005, decisions 5 and 7; docs/adr/0090).
#
# Run with
# `scripts/mutate sce-build/tests/mutations/a_kotlin_host_invoke_completion_naming_its_origin_needs_no_engine_kotlin.cases`.
#
# An invocation the host serves reports how it ended naming its origin: a Mesh router
# names the peer that answered (SCE_MESH.md §9.5). The engine used to take any event
# that named an origin for one from an invoked child and look for the `<finalize>`
# that child's invoke declared, which is script text, and so asked for a script engine
# before it asked whether there was anything to run. A machine of
# `datamodel="sce-static"` has no engine and no `<finalize>`, so the first answer a real
# router gave it threw "scriptEngine is required ... codegen invariant" out of `tick()`.
#
# docs/adr/0090 split the two readers of that one string: the origin is the reply
# address the document reads, and the invocation an event came from is found by its
# `sender`, which only the SCXML Event I/O Processor sets. A host's ending names an
# origin and no sender, so it no longer reaches the finalize lookup at all, and
# `AStaticMeshRequestReachesTheRouterTest`, which fails a request naming `mesh://motor`,
# stays green under the mutant below: the question the mutant moves is not asked of
# it. The guard still answers for the events that do name a sender on a machine with
# no engine: an invoked child's. `static_invoke_tree` is such a machine, and in
# `AChildSessionsHostInvocationIsServedByTheTreesHostTest` its child, once the host
# ends the child's clock, tells its parent `stamped`, which the engine-less root takes.
# The mutant puts the engine back in front of the question, and that test turns red.
#
# What keeps a host's ending out of the lookup is the sender check above the guard. A
# mutant that read the origin's address as the sender again (the shape docs/adr/0090
# removed) is not a case here: on a machine with no `<finalize>` the guard behind it
# returns as well, so it is unobservable rather than unguarded.
#
# Anchors are literal slices of the source; an edit that moves one is reported
# INCONCLUSIVE with the anchor quoted, never as a pass.

mutation_gradle . :sce-kotlin-tests:test --tests 'com.sce.integration.AChildSessionsHostInvocationIsServedByTheTreesHostTest' --tests 'com.sce.integration.AStaticMeshRequestReachesTheRouterTest'
mutation_targets backends/kotlin/runtime/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/sce/runtime/StateMachineEngine.kt
mutation_oracles backends/kotlin/tests/src/test/kotlin/com/sce/integration/AChildSessionsHostInvocationIsServedByTheTreesHostTest.kt sce-build/tests/fixtures/static_datamodel/static_invoke_tree.scxml backends/kotlin/tests/src/test/kotlin/com/sce/integration/AStaticMeshRequestReachesTheRouterTest.kt sce-build/tests/fixtures/host_processor/statechart_static_mesh_request.scxml

mutation_case "an event naming its sender asks for an engine before asking for a finalize" <<'PY'
edit("backends/kotlin/runtime/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/sce/runtime/StateMachineEngine.kt",
     "        if (activeInvokes.values.none { it.finalizeScript.isNotEmpty() }) return\n",
     "        if (false && activeInvokes.values.none { it.finalizeScript.isNotEmpty() }) return\n")
PY
